      "output": "At its most fundamental level, **water** is a chemical compound and one of the most abundant and essential substances on Earth. \n\nHere is a breakdown of what water is, looking at it through different lenses:\n\n### 1. The Chemical View\n* **Formula:** $H_2O$\n* **Composition:** Each molecule of water is made up of **two hydrogen atoms** bonded to **one oxygen atom**.\n* **State of Matter:** Water is famous for being the only natural substance on Earth that exists abundantly in three physical states: \n  * **Liquid** (the water we drink, rivers, oceans)\n  * **Solid** (ice, snow, glaciers)\n  * **Gas** (water vapor, steam, humidity)\n\n### 2. Physical and Chemical Properties\nWater has several unique and unusual properties that make it vital for life:\n* **The \"Universal Solvent\":** Water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. Because of this, it easily carries nutrients, chemicals, and minerals wherever it goes.\n* **Cohesion and Adhesion:** Water molecules like to stick to each other (cohesion—which creates surface tension, allowing some insects to walk on water) and to other surfaces (adhesion—which helps water move up the roots of plants).\n* **High Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb and release large amounts of heat with only small changes in its own temperature. This helps regulate the climate of the Earth and the body temperatures of living organisms.\n* **Density Anomaly:** Most substances shrink and become denser when they freeze, but water actually *expands* and becomes less dense. That is why ice floats on water.\n\n### 3. The Ecological and Biological View\n* **The Source of Life:** All known forms of life depend on water. It acts as the medium inside cells where metabolic and chemical reactions take place.\n* **Earth’s Lifeblood:** Often called the \"Blue Planet,\" about **71% of Earth's surface is covered by water**, mostly in oceans (about 96.5% of all Earth's water is salt water). \n* **The Water Cycle:** Water is constantly recycled through evaporation, condensation, precipitation (rain and snow), and collection, meaning the water you drink today is the same water that dinosaurs drank millions of years ago.\n\nIn short, water is a simple molecule that possesses miraculous properties, acting as the foundation for weather, geology,"
